+## `tube-stacker` (2026-09-29): "copy image" preference extends past charts to a game's result screen
+The `tube-tetris`/`tube-stacker` thread's iteration 2 asked for a graph copy-
+image button (already recorded above); a later message in the same thread
+asked separately for "a generated results image to be copied and shared" on
+the game itself — i.e. a game-over screen, not a chart. Read together: this
+requester's "always give us a big shiny copy image button" preference isn't
+scoped to charts/diagrams specifically, it's **any page that produces a
+result worth sharing** (a score, a finished game, a generated artifact).
+Built here as a canvas snapshot of the live 3D view composited with score
+text, with the same prominent gradient-button treatment as the Venn-diagram
+copy button. Durable: default to a shareable copy-image affordance on any
+future build with a "you're done, here's your result" moment, not only ones
+with a literal chart.
+
+Also reconfirms two already-recorded rules held on a from-scratch rebuild:
+"block manipulation" keys (arrows/WASD) stayed conceptually separate from
+camera drag controls without needing a fresh correction, and "all the
+normal features" for a named genre was read as the full expected set
+(pause button included, reasoning from the kit's own "a site whose whole
+point is movement should offer its own pause" guidance, not from anything
+this requester said directly — worth watching whether they comment on it).
